# A host-driven frog's attacks all play on the client's copy too: spit, tongue and mortar follow each other
# fast, and the copy plays the host's swing late. Over a jittery link it used to cut a third of them off mid
# wind-up to start the next, so those blows never landed. Now the next swing waits for the wind-up to end.
# The client stands back and watches the frogs fight the host: a creature fighting the client itself thinks on the
# client's machine and replays nothing (fighter.coop).

include session_net.coop
# Invincible: the frog swamp attacks idle players, and both down at once ends the run.
A run invincibility
B run invincibility
set frog1 688b0e3e-0189-4f5b-9b42-30dba420ba5f

A tpnear $frog1 150 0
B tpnear $frog1 420 40
A expect dead $frog1 == "0 loaded" timeout=20
B expect dead $frog1 == "0 loaded" timeout=20
# They come at the host on their own; the client's copies replay every swing the host's frogs start.
A expect counter swingsannounced >= 40 timeout=90
B expect counter swingsreplayed >= 20 timeout=5
B expect counter transitionsmissed <= 2 timeout=1
B expect counter cutshort <= 4 timeout=1
B expect counter swingsdropped <= 0 timeout=1

# ---- The ranged frog's mortar lands on the AI's target, which the client's copy (AI off) only knows from the host. ----
A hit Frog_Ranged 1
B expect counter aimed >= 1 timeout=40
